# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) for local work. In production these are Worker
# secrets and bindings, not a file — `wrangler secret put`, see CLAUDE.md's
# deployment runbook. (The deployed shape is a Worker, not Pages.)
#
# Everything except PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY is read at request time from the
# Worker's bindings, never from `import.meta.env` — see src/lib/runtime-env.ts
# for why. In `astro dev` the Cloudflare adapter's platform proxy loads this
# file into those bindings for you ("Using secrets defined in .env" on start).
#
# The endpoint refuses to run — 503, with the phone number as the fallback —
# if any of the five secrets below is missing. A bot check or a rate limit that
# quietly disables itself when unconfigured is worse than not having one.
#
# `.env` is NOT what the Playwright suite runs against. Once real keys live
# here, feeding them to the local Worker would make the bot check reject the
# suite's dummy token and would make the JavaScript-off form post send a real
# email on every run. The suite reads the committed `.env.test` instead, and
# tests/prepare-worker.ts refuses to fall back to this file.

# --- Turnstile (PRD §6.5) ---------------------------------------------------
# The values below are Cloudflare's own publicly documented test keys. The site
# key renders a visible widget that always passes; the secret always verifies.
# They are here so the form works on a clean checkout. REPLACE BOTH before any
# real deployment — with these in place there is no bot check at all.
PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA

# --- Resend (PRD §8) --------------------------------------------------------
RESEND_API_KEY=re_replace_me

# Where the enquiry lands. This is an unsolicited concept: it must NEVER be the
# practice's real inbox (info@coventrydental.co.uk). Use your own address.
ENQUIRY_TO_EMAIL=you@example.com

# A sender on a domain verified in Resend. Resend rejects anything else.
ENQUIRY_FROM_EMAIL=Coventry Dental Concept <enquiries@example.com>

# --- Rate limit (PRD §6.4) --------------------------------------------------
# Salt for the SHA-256 of the client IP. Any long random string; changing it
# resets every open window. The IP itself is never stored.
ENQUIRY_IP_SALT=replace-with-a-long-random-string

# --- Not a variable: the KV binding -----------------------------------------
# The rate limit reads a KV namespace bound as ENQUIRY_RATE_LIMIT. It cannot
# come from this file — it is declared in wrangler.jsonc and created with
# `wrangler kv namespace create ENQUIRY_RATE_LIMIT`. Unbound, the endpoint
# counts in memory, logs a warning, and keeps working — but per-isolate, so
# that is a development convenience and not a real limit.
